      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A hybrid approach that prioritizes highest local need while offering a lottery for waitlisted applicants generally ensures the greatest equity. This method can first target households passing specific income thresholds before rotating among those qualify for transit-proximate units needed for employment. Integrating clear criteria for each category and a public appeal process will help resolve disputes and build community trust. Ultimately, flexibility allows the district to address both immediate accessibility and long-term success for residents.",
      "source": "target",
